Package Responsibility <code>fleet</code> The fleet document's types, loading, validation and schema; units, users and paths derived from names <code>schema</code> The fleet and zones documents' generated JSON Schemas, embedded <code>release</code>, <code>provenance</code> Package a clean, tagged checkout into an archive with its revision and checksum; name upstream commits <code>deploy/target</code> Resolve an app stack to its host, unit, user, paths and ports <code>deploy/secrets</code>, <code>deploy/secrets/awsssm</code> Read a stack's prefix into environment, migrate-only variables and key files, and mask them; AWS SSM <code>deploy/archive</code> Verify an archive and extract it safely <code>deploy/deployer</code> The operator side: build the request, dial the stack's host, transfer, run on the host, record <code>deploy/onhost</code> The host side: lock, unpack, install, validate, migrate, switch, health, restore, prune, audit <code>deploy/ship</code> Package a tag or local commit in a temporary worktree with the app's release script <code>deploy/unpushed</code> The commits each live release was built from that are on no remote branch of their checkout <code>deploy/readiness</code> Check every host name's <code>/readyz</code> from outside <code>deploy/hooks</code> Run the operator's hooks around packaging, deploy and rollback <code>deploy/hostaddr</code> Resolve a host's or server's address, and Pulumi configuration values <code>deploy/systemd</code>, <code>deploy/host</code> Render units and their sandbox, and the idempotent host-setup script <code>deploy/caddy</code>, <code>deploy/cfranges</code> Render a host's Caddyfile; Cloudflare's published proxy ranges <code>ledger</code> Append and read the per-stack JSON Lines ledger <code>tlsmin</code> A host's minimum TLS version, checked from outside <code>zones</code>, <code>zoneharden</code> The zones document and its verification; the security baseline through Cloudflare's API <code>origincert</code> Issue, list and revoke origin certificates, made on the host <code>dbroles</code>, <code>dbsnapshot</code> Database and role plans with SCRAM verifiers and connection limits; snapshots of a Lightsail server <code>dbcopy</code> A stack's databases copied to another server, row counts compared, and its parameters promoted <code>dbimport</code> A data-only dump loaded into a stack's database as its owner, in one transaction <code>hostports</code> A Lightsail instance's firewall checked against the CDN's ranges and the admin addresses <code>deployrunbook</code> A live stack's recurring deploy runbook <code>runbookkit</code> Remote quoting, install-from-console actions, permission lists, step needs, inputs and fixes for a tool's own runbooks <code>fleetpage</code> The fleet's inventory page and the fleet document's format reference <code>credpage</code> One app stack's credentials as an HTML page <code>deploy/preflight</code> Before a deploy, the registry's secrets under the stack's prefix checked by name in the parameter store <code>stackiam</code> Each stack's parameter-store IAM policy and operators' group: plan, apply, verify <code>cli</code> The Cobra command tree, mountable by a host tool <p>Load and check a fleet document with the <code>fleet</code> package:</p> <pre><code>f, err := fleet.Load("fleet.json")
if err != nil {
    return err
}
app, stack, err := f.Stack("example-app", "prod")
</code></pre>
